3. How Private Attributes Work (Name Mangling)
 * Direct Access Attempt: Writing L1.__rpm = 99999 creates a new, unrelated attribute called __rpm on L1; it does not overwrite the internal private variable.
 * True Internal Name: Python renames double-underscore attributes internally to _ClassName__attribute (e.g., _Lathe__rpm).
 * True Override (Name Mangling Bypass): Accessing L1._Lathe__rpm reaches the actual private variable.
> Python's Philosophy ("We are all consenting adults"): Double underscores do not lock the door—they move the handle somewhere awkward. Guards prevent accidental misuse, but an operator who explicitly types _Lathe__rpm intentionally removes the guard.
